# E §3.1 step 1: "a member that is itself a joint model pins its own members through its use lines", and "A joint
# model's imports are checked against their hashes (LOAD-PIN)": member a's own pin of b doesn't match b, so a is
# refused, and with it the joint model (L §6.1 "A file that doesn't match its hash is refused").
=== J/joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "../A" sha256 "84d429791e5712d3942ddb98bc323da22c2a6fb3ff9bb36dbe6e9ebec3b2b3d1"

ask r: a.rate
=== A/reality.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use b = "../B" sha256 "1111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111"

source s "umowa"

input rate: num

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  rate = 0.12 "umowa"
=== B/reality.tally
model ben
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
=== expect
refused: member a: LOAD-PIN ../B doesn't match its sha256 in use b
